IMPORT prelude

-- Supplementary Supply (FY 2025) Act 2026 (Singapore, No. 7 of 2026) -- what "FY 2025" means (s 2), the further sums authorised
-- from the Consolidated Fund (s 3) and the Development Fund (s 4), and the Schedule of Heads of Expenditure they are appropriated to.
--
-- Edition: informal consolidation, "version in force from 20/3/2026", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SSFY2025A2026.txt (SSO marks it "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The deposit annotates no
-- amendment and lists no historical versions.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0221 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. The honest answer is: nothing directly. It is an appropriation Act. It authorises the Government to issue
-- money and says for which Heads; it gives no person a right, duty, fee, deadline or offence.
--
-- The whole Act is encoded (ss 2-4 and the Schedule). Not encoded: s 1 (short title), and anything the Act takes from elsewhere --
-- the Supply Act 2025 it supplements, the Constitution's rules on supply, and the Financial Procedure Act. None was read here.
--
-- The SCHEDULE is a column-shifted PDF table. Its 11 rows of figures were matched to its 11 Heads BY ORDER, not by the visual line
-- they sit on. That matching is an inference. It is supported by the arithmetic: on that matching each row's two columns add up to
-- its total, and the columns add up to the s 3 and s 4 sums exactly (asserted in the case file). The column sums would also hold under
-- other labellings, so they do not prove which Head carries which figure.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md. NOT for public use.

§ `Supplementary Supply (FY 2025) Act 2026`

-- The Heads named in the Schedule, with their letters, plus one value for any Head the Schedule does not name.
DECLARE Head IS ONE OF
    `B Attorney-General's Chambers`
    `E Judicature`
    `I Ministry of Social and Family Development`
    `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment`
    `P Ministry of Home Affairs`
    `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information`
    `S Ministry of Manpower`
    `T Ministry of National Development`
    `V Ministry of Trade and Industry`
    `W Ministry of Transport`
    `Z Financial Transfers`
    `a Head not specified in the Schedule`

DECLARE Fund IS ONE OF
    `the Consolidated Fund`
    `the Development Fund`
    `some other fund`

§§ `2 -- FY 2025`

-- s 2: "'FY 2025' means the period starting 1 April 2025 and ending 31 March 2026."
-- Both ends are inside the period. A date is given as year, month and day.
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the date key` IS `year` * 10000 + `month` * 100 + `day`

GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER, `month` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the date falls in FY 2025` IF
        `the date key` `year` `month` `day` >= 20250401
    AND `the date key` `year` `month` `day` <= 20260331

§§ `3 -- supplementary supply from the Consolidated Fund`

-- s 3(1): "A further sum of not more than $1,087,355,800, not otherwise provided for by the Supply Act 2025, is authorised to be
-- issued from the Consolidated Fund for FY 2025."
-- (2): "The sum in subsection (1) is appropriated for the Heads of Expenditure for the public service specified in the Schedule."
`the Consolidated Fund ceiling` MEANS 1087355800

§§ `4 -- supplementary supply from the Development Fund`

-- s 4(1): "A further sum of not more than $2,161,019,900, not otherwise provided for by the Supply Act 2025, is authorised to be
-- issued from the Development Fund for FY 2025."
-- (2): "The sum in subsection (1) is appropriated for development purposes under the Heads of Expenditure specified in the Schedule."
`the Development Fund ceiling` MEANS 2161019900

-- The authority is to issue a further sum "for FY 2025", "not otherwise provided for by the Supply Act 2025", up to the ceiling for
-- that fund. Whether a sum is otherwise provided for by the Supply Act 2025 is a fact this encoding takes as given; that Act was not
-- read. The Act authorises issue from only these two funds.
GIVEN `the fund` IS A Fund
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the ceiling for` IS
    CONSIDER `the fund`
    WHEN `the Consolidated Fund` THEN `the Consolidated Fund ceiling`
    WHEN `the Development Fund` THEN `the Development Fund ceiling`
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the fund` IS A Fund, `the further sum` IS A NUMBER, `is for FY 2025` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `already provided for by the Supply Act 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the issue is authorised by this Act` IF
        `is for FY 2025`
    AND (NOT `already provided for by the Supply Act 2025`)
    AND `the further sum` > 0
    AND `the further sum` <= `the ceiling for` `the fund`

§§ `The Schedule -- Heads of Expenditure for which further sums are appropriated`

-- The Schedule ("Sections 3(2) and 4(2)") has the columns "Appropriation from Consolidated Fund", "Appropriation from Development
-- Fund" and "Total appropriations". "..." in a column means nothing from that fund. Figures in dollars, matched to Heads BY ORDER (see
-- the header):
--   B Attorney-General's Chambers                         ...         364,800         364,800
--   E Judicature                                   16,486,700             ...      16,486,700
--   I Ministry of Social and Family Development           ...      31,226,800      31,226,800
--   L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment 66,598,800    16,361,800      82,960,600
--   P Ministry of Home Affairs                    472,103,300             ...     472,103,300
--   Q Ministry of Digital Development and Info'n          ...      44,183,300      44,183,300
--   S Ministry of Manpower                        346,483,200      22,275,000     368,758,200
--   T Ministry of National Development                    ...     909,322,000     909,322,000
--   V Ministry of Trade and Industry               26,336,400             ...      26,336,400
--   W Ministry of Transport                       131,183,600   1,137,286,200   1,268,469,800
--   Z Financial Transfers                          28,163,800             ...      28,163,800
--   Total                                       1,087,355,800   2,161,019,900   3,248,375,700
GIVEN `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` IS
    CONSIDER `the head`
    WHEN `E Judicature` THEN 16486700
    WHEN `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment` THEN 66598800
    WHEN `P Ministry of Home Affairs` THEN 472103300
    WHEN `S Ministry of Manpower` THEN 346483200
    WHEN `V Ministry of Trade and Industry` THEN 26336400
    WHEN `W Ministry of Transport` THEN 131183600
    WHEN `Z Financial Transfers` THEN 28163800
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Development Fund appropriation for` IS
    CONSIDER `the head`
    WHEN `B Attorney-General's Chambers` THEN 364800
    WHEN `I Ministry of Social and Family Development` THEN 31226800
    WHEN `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment` THEN 16361800
    WHEN `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information` THEN 44183300
    WHEN `S Ministry of Manpower` THEN 22275000
    WHEN `T Ministry of National Development` THEN 909322000
    WHEN `W Ministry of Transport` THEN 1137286200
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the head` IS A Head, `the fund` IS A Fund
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the appropriation for` IS
    CONSIDER `the fund`
    WHEN `the Consolidated Fund` THEN `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `the head`
    WHEN `the Development Fund` THEN `the Development Fund appropriation for` `the head`
    OTHERWISE 0

-- The "Total appropriations" column, computed. The case file checks it against the printed totals.
GIVEN `the head` IS A Head
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the total appropriation for` IS
    `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `the head` + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `the head`

-- Inference, not stated in the Act: a further sum appropriated "for the Heads ... specified in the Schedule" can be spent under a Head
-- only up to that Head's figure in the column for that fund, and not at all under a Head the Schedule does not name.
GIVEN `the head` IS A Head, `the fund` IS A Fund, `the amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the amount is within the Head's supplementary appropriation` IF
        `the amount` > 0
    AND `the amount` <= `the appropriation for` `the head` `the fund`

-- The Schedule's column totals, computed from the rows.
`the Consolidated Fund column total` MEANS
      `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `B Attorney-General's Chambers`
    + `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `E Judicature`
    + `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `I Ministry of Social and Family Development`
    + `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment`
    + `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `P Ministry of Home Affairs`
    + `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information`
    + `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `S Ministry of Manpower`
    + `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `T Ministry of National Development`
    + `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `V Ministry of Trade and Industry`
    + `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `W Ministry of Transport`
    + `the Consolidated Fund appropriation for` `Z Financial Transfers`

`the Development Fund column total` MEANS
      `the Development Fund appropriation for` `B Attorney-General's Chambers`
    + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `E Judicature`
    + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `I Ministry of Social and Family Development`
    + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `L Ministry of Sustainability and the Environment`
    + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `P Ministry of Home Affairs`
    + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `Q Ministry of Digital Development and Information`
    + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `S Ministry of Manpower`
    + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `T Ministry of National Development`
    + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `V Ministry of Trade and Industry`
    + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `W Ministry of Transport`
    + `the Development Fund appropriation for` `Z Financial Transfers`

`the grand total` MEANS `the Consolidated Fund column total` + `the Development Fund column total`
